      "text": "To simplify \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we start by letting \\(z = \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\). We need to find the value of \\(z + \\frac{1}{z}\\).\n\nFirst, we compute \\(z \\cdot \\overline{z}\\) where \\(\\overline{z} = \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\) is the conjugate of \\(z\\).\n\n\\[\nz = \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(z \\cdot \\overline{z}\\), we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n\\[\nz \\cdot \\overline{z} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the denominator:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\n\nCalculating the numerator:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\nz \\cdot \\overline{z} = \\frac{34}{34} = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the property of reciprocals to find \\(z + \\frac{1}{z}\\):\n\n\\[\nz + \\frac{1}{z} = \\frac{z}{z} + \\frac{\\overline{z}}{\\overline{z}} = \\frac{z}{1} + \\frac{\\overline{z}}{1} = z + \\overline{z}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(z\\) and \\(z^* = \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\) are complex conjugates, their sum is real:\n\n\\[\nz + \\overline{z} = \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\n\\]\n\nThus, \n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = 1 + 1 = 2\n\\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
