      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we can use the property of Euler's formula, which states that \\(e^{i\\theta} = \\cos \\theta + i \\sin \\theta\\). We will first express each complex fraction in polar form and then add the two results.\n\n**Step 1: Convert each fraction to polar form.**\n\nFor \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\):\n\n- The magnitude \\(r_1\\) is \\(\\sqrt{3^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 25} = \\sqrt{34}\\).\n- The argument \\(\\theta_1\\) is \\(\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)\\).\n\nSo, \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{\\sqrt{34} e^{i \\theta_1}} = \\sqrt{34} e^{-i \\theta_1}\\).\n\nFor \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\):\n\n- The magnitude \\(r_2\\) is \\(\\sqrt{3^2 + (-5)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 25} = \\sqrt{34}\\).\n- The argument \\(\\theta_2\\) is \\(\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{-5}{3}\\right)\\), which is \\(-\\theta_1\\).\n\nSo, \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{\\sqrt{34} e^{-i \\theta_1}} = \\sqrt{34} e^{i \\theta_1}\\).\n\n**Step 2: Add the two complex numbers in polar form.**\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we have:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{34} e^{-i \\theta_1} + \\sqrt{34} e^{i \\theta_1} = \\sqrt{34} \\left( e^{-i \\theta_1} + e^{i \\theta_1} \\right).\n\\]\n\nUsing the identity \\(e^{i \\theta_1} + e^{-i \\theta_1} = 2 \\cos \\theta_1\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{34} e^{-i \\theta_1} + \\sqrt{34} e^{i \\theta_1} = \\sqrt{34} \\cdot 2 \\cos \\theta_1 = 2 \\sqrt{34} \\cos \\theta_1.\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Convert back to rectangular form.**\n\nUsing the values of \\(\\cos \\theta_1\\) and \\(\\theta_1\\) from the given components of the fractions, we have:\n- The magnitude is \\(r = 2\\).\n- The phase shift is \\(\\theta = \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)/2\\).\n\nThus,\n\\[\n2 \\sqrt{34} \\cos \\theta_1 = 2 \\sqrt{34} \\cdot \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{34}} = 10.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}.\n\\]",
