      "text": "The first thing we can observe when tackling problems with complex numbers is to start simplifying. At first, we will split up the problem into two (later, more complicated) parts: simplifying\n\\[\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \\quad\\text{and}\\quad \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}.\\]After this step, we will add the two objects together and simplify. We will need to use some Python code to help us simplify the numerators. \nLet's start by tackling the first part. First, multiply the top and bottom by $3 + 5i.$ This will give us:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} &= \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{3^2 - 5^2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9 + 30i + 25i^2}{9 - 25} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9 + 30i - 25}{36 - 25} \\\\\n&= -1 - \\frac{3}{4}i.\n\\end{align*}\nNow, we will do the exact same thing for the second part. After multiplying the top and bottom of $\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}$ by $3 - 5i,$ we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} &= \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{3^2 - 5^2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9 - 30i + 25i^2}{9 - 25} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9 - 30i - 25}{-16} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-16 - 30i}{25} \\\\\n&= -\\frac{16}{25} - \\frac{3}{5}i.\n\\end{align*}\nNow that we have simplified the two parts above, we must add them together:\n\\begin{align*}\n-1 - \\frac{3}{4}i + \\left( -\\frac{16}{25} - \\frac{3}{5}i \\right) &= -\\left( 1 + \\frac{16}{25} \\right) - \\frac{3}{4}i - \\frac{3}{5}i \\\\\n&= -\\frac{41}{25} - \\frac{9}{20}i.\n\\end{align*}\nWe have now simplified the problem. Our final answer is: $-\\boxed{-\\frac{41}{25}-\\frac{9}{20}i}.$\nThe final answer is: -\\frac{41}{25}-\\frac{9}{20}i",
